# Dear ImGui pin — SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH.
#
# Sourced by `setup_imgui.sh` and by `.github/workflows/ci.yml`. Bump the
# commit here and every consumer follows; there is no second copy to forget.
#
# Why the `docking` branch and not `master`: POM2 hosts a DockSpace so its 38
# panels become tabs in a persistent layout instead of a pile of overlapping
# windows (MainWindow::renderDockSpace / applyDockLayout). Docking lives only
# on this branch — `IMGUI_HAS_DOCK` is not defined on master, and the build
# fails at `ImGuiConfigFlags_DockingEnable`. Despite the branch name it is
# what most Dear ImGui applications ship; upstream rebases it on master
# regularly.
#
# Multi-viewport (the branch's other feature) is deliberately left OFF — see
# the ConfigFlags comment in main.cpp.
#
# Why pinned to a commit and not just the branch: `docking` is force-pushed on
# every rebase, so an unpinned shallow clone makes the build non-reproducible
# and lets CI break on an upstream change we never made.
IMGUI_REPO=https://github.com/ocornut/imgui.git
IMGUI_BRANCH=docking
IMGUI_COMMIT=b334d19b667958ed970000073644d911fae17e57
# Human-readable version reported by the pinned commit (imgui.h IMGUI_VERSION).
IMGUI_VERSION=1.92.9
